result: {"findings":[{"topic":"React CRUD with Hooks — Core Pattern","summary":"The canonical pattern uses useState for three pieces of state: items array, currentItem (for editing), and an editing boolean. Add/delete/update functions mutate the array via functional updates (map/filter/spread). Edit mode conditionally renders either AddForm or EditForm in the same panel. useEffect syncs the edit form when currentItem changes.","source":"https://www.taniarascia.com/crud-app-in-react-with-hooks/","relevance":"high","codeExample":"const [products, setProducts] = useState<Product[]>(initialData);
const [currentProduct, setCurrentProduct] = useState<Product | null>(null);
const [editing, setEditing] = useState(false);

const addProduct = (p: Omit<Product,'id'>) =>
  setProducts(prev => [...prev, { ...p, id: crypto.randomUUID() }]);

const updateProduct = (id: string, updated: Product) =>
  setProducts(prev => prev.map(p => p.id === id ? updated : p));

const deleteProduct = (id: string) =>
  setProducts(prev => prev.filter(p => p.id !== id));","codeExampleLang":"typescript"},{"topic":"TypeScript Product Interface + In-Memory API Service","summary":"Define a Product interface with id (string UUID), name (string), price (number), category (string). The mock API service wraps in-memory array in async functions (returning Promise<T>) so it can be swapped for a real API later. Use crypto.randomUUID() for IDs (supported in all modern browsers and Node 14.17+). Export singleton instance or standalone functions.","source":"https://blog.logrocket.com/react-typescript-how-type-hooks-complete-guide/","relevance":"high","codeExample":"// src/services/api.ts
export interface Product {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  price: number;
  category: string;
}

let store: Product[] = [
  { id: '1', name: 'Widget A', price: 9.99, category: 'Widgets' },
];

export const api = {
  getAll: (): Promise<Product[]> => Promise.resolve([...store]),
  create: (p: Omit<Product,'id'>): Promise<Product> => {
    const product = { ...p, id: crypto.randomUUID() };
    store = [...store, product];
    return Promise.resolve(product);
  },
  update: (id: string, p: Partial<Product>): Promise<Product> => {
    store = store.map(x => x.id === id ? { ...x, ...p } : x);
    const updated = store.find(x => x.id === id)!;
    return Promise.resolve(updated);
  },
  remove: (id: string): Promise<void> => {
    store = store.filter(x => x.id !== id);
    return Promise.resolve();
  },
};","codeExampleLang":"typescript"},{"topic":"Form Validation Pattern (React + TypeScript)","summary":"Keep errors as Partial<Record<keyof FormFields, string>>. Validate on submit: check required fields, price > 0, name non-empty. Display error messages under each input. The form should NOT submit if any error exists. Use controlled inputs with onChange updating a single state object via computed property name (event.target.name as keyof type).","source":"https://dev.to/finiam/react-hooks-and-typescript-a-practical-guide-52f5","relevance":"high","codeExample":"type FormErrors = Partial<Record<keyof ProductForm, string>>;

const validate = (form: ProductForm): FormErrors => {
  const errors: FormErrors = {};
  if (!form.name.trim()) errors.name = 'Name is required';
  if (!form.category.trim()) errors.category = 'Category is required';
  const price = Number(form.price);
  if (isNaN(price) || price <= 0) errors.price = 'Price must be a positive number';
  return errors;
};

const handleSubmit = (e: React.FormEvent) => {
  e.preventDefault();
  const errs = validate(form);
  if (Object.keys(errs).length > 0) { setErrors(errs); return; }
  onSubmit(form);
};","codeExampleLang":"typescript"},{"topic":"ProductList Table Component Structure","summary":"Render a <table> with thead showing Name, Price, Category, Actions columns. In tbody, map products to rows. Price should be formatted with toLocaleString('en-US', { style: 'currency', currency: 'USD' }). Each row has Edit (calls onEdit(product)) and Delete (calls onDelete(product.id)) buttons. Show empty state row when products.length === 0. Accept typed props interface.","source":"https://www.taniarascia.com/crud-app-in-react-with-hooks/","relevance":"high","codeExample":"interface ProductListProps {
  products: Product[];
  onEdit: (product: Product) => void;
  onDelete: (id: string) => void;
}

export const ProductList: React.FC<ProductListProps> = ({ products, onEdit, onDelete }) => (
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Price</th><th>Category</th><th>Actions</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {products.length === 0 ? (
        <tr><td colSpan={4}>No products found.</td></tr>
      ) : products.map(p => (
        <tr key={p.id}>
          <td>{p.name}</td>
          <td>{p.price.toLocaleString('en-US',{style:'currency',currency:'USD'})}</td>
          <td>{p.category}</td>
          <td>
            <button onClick={() => onEdit(p)}>Edit</button>
            <button onClick={() => onDelete(p.id)}>Delete</button>
          </td>
        </tr>
      ))}
    </tbody>
  </table>
);","codeExampleLang":"typescript"},{"topic":"App Orchestration — useEffect for async API calls","summary":"Load initial data with useEffect + async IIFE on mount. Wrap all api calls in useCallback to keep references stable. Track loading/error state for production-readiness even with mock API. The editing flow: clicking Edit sets editing=true and currentProduct; the conditional JSX in the form panel swaps AddProduct ↔ EditProduct; Cancel resets editing=false.","source":"https://www.taniarascia.com/crud-app-in-react-with-hooks/","relevance":"high","codeExample":"useEffect(() => {
  (async () => {
    const data = await api.getAll();
    setProducts(data);
  })();
}, []);

const handleAdd = useCallback(async (form: ProductForm) => {
  const created = await api.create(form);
  setProducts(prev => [...prev, created]);
}, []);

const handleUpdate = useCallback(async (id: string, form: ProductForm) => {
  const updated = await api.update(id, form);
  setProducts(prev => prev.map(p => p.id === id ? updated : p));
  setEditing(false);
  setCurrentProduct(null);
}, []);

const handleDelete = useCallback(async (id: string) => {
  await api.remove(id);
  setProducts(prev => prev.filter(p => p.id !== id));
}, []);","codeExampleLang":"typescript"}],"recommendations":["File structure: src/services/api.ts (mock service), src/types/product.ts (Product interface + ProductForm type), src/components/ProductList.tsx, src/components/ProductForm.tsx (handles both add and edit via props), src/App.tsx (state orchestration).","Use a single ProductForm component for both Add and Edit: it accepts an optional initialValues prop. When initialValues is provided, it pre-fills the form fields and changes the submit button label to 'Update'. useEffect(() => { if (initialValues) setForm(initialValues); }, [initialValues]) handles switching between edit targets.","Define price as string in form state (ProductForm type) and convert to number only on submit/validation — this prevents NaN issues with controlled number inputs. Parse with parseFloat and validate > 0.","Keep the in-memory store as a module-level let variable in api.ts (not exported directly). All mutation goes through the api functions. This makes swapping to a real HTTP client trivial — just replace the function bodies.","Use crypto.randomUUID() for IDs — available natively in browsers and Node 14.17+. No uuid package needed.","For edit flow: when user clicks Edit on a row, call setCurrentProduct(product) and setEditing(true). Show <ProductForm initialValues={currentProduct} onSubmit={handleUpdate} onCancel={() => setEditing(false)} /> conditionally. When not editing, show <ProductForm onSubmit={handleAdd} />.","Wrap handleAdd, handleUpdate, handleDelete in useCallback with empty deps (they only close over setter functions which are stable). This prevents unnecessary re-renders of memoized child components.","For the category field, consider either a free-text input or a <select> with predefined options — either works, but a select prevents typos and inconsistent casing that would cause grouping issues if you later add category filtering."],"warnings":["crypto.randomUUID() is not available in non-secure contexts (HTTP, not HTTPS) in some browsers. For local dev this is fine; for production ensure HTTPS.","The in-memory API store is module-level state — it resets on page refresh. This is expected for a mock, but document it clearly.","If EditProductForm uses useEffect to sync initialValues, add initialValues to the dep array. Missing this means switching between editing two different products won't update the form.","Price is a number in the Product type but inputs always return strings — always parse/validate before storing. Using type='number' on the input helps but doesn't prevent empty string submission.","The taniarascia tutorial is from 2019 and uses plain JS — the patterns are sound but do not copy the code verbatim. Key TypeScript adaptations: add generic types to useState<Product[]>([]), type event handlers as React.ChangeEvent<HTMLInputElement>, type form submit as React.FormEvent<HTMLFormElement>.","Do not use index as key for mapped list items — use product.id. Index keys break React reconciliation when items are deleted from the middle of the array."]}}
