) in some browsers. For local dev this is fine; for production ensure HTTPS.","The in-memory API store is module-level state — it resets on page refresh. This is expected for a mock, but document it clearly.","If EditProductForm uses useEffect to sync initialValues, add initialValues to the dep array. Missing this means switching between editing two different products won't update the form.","Price is a number in the Product type but inputs always return strings — always parse/validate before storing. Using type='number' on the input helps but doesn't prevent empty string submission.","The taniarascia tutorial is from 2019 and uses plain JS — the patterns are sound but do not copy the code verbatim. Key TypeScript adaptations: add generic types to useState<Product[]>([]), type event handlers as React.ChangeEvent<HTMLInputElement>, type form submit as React.FormEvent<HTMLFormElement>.","Do not use index as key for mapped list items — use product.id. Index keys break React reconciliation when items are deleted from the middle of the array."]}}
